      "featured": true,
      "description": "My artistic practice explores form, lettering, character, and the visual language of contemporary urban culture. Drawing from graffiti, street culture, graphic design, comics, and popular media, I combine familiar visual elements into new structures.\n\nAt the center of my work is a recurring male character, developed from my graffiti practice in 2014–2015. He embodies the tension between traditional values and contemporary urban life — a person whose body belongs to the present, while his mindset remains rooted in the past.\n\nThrough constantly changing techniques, colors, and styles, I use this character to explore identity, cultural heritage, social expectations, and the conflict between tradition and change.",
